{"title":"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose a square piece of paper is folded in half vertically.  The folded paper is then cut in half along the dashed line.  Three rectangles are formed-a large one and two small ones.  What is the ratio of the perimeter of one of the small rectangles to the perimeter of the large rectangle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/8/9f88225a0c24d20641c9a40e783abf607b4fd95f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ \\frac{3}{4} \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ \\frac{4}{5} \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ \\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"349\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/b/6ab13c6ad222a415ca8ff4bfb6135d981e1c657c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(0,8)--(6,8)--(6,0)--cycle); draw((0,8)--(5,9)--(5,8)); draw((3,-1.5)--(3,10.3),dashed); draw((0,5.5)..(-.75,4.75)..(0,4)); draw((0,4)--(1.5,4),EndArrow); [/asy]\" width=\"145\" height=\"252\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In this diagram, the dashed segment is the fold while the blue segments are cuts.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/7/13711e5473de3200686f84f3d375cb224663fe3e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(4,0)--(4,4)--(0,4)--cycle,linewidth(1)); draw((1,0)--(1,4),blue+linewidth(1)); draw((2,0)--(2,4),dashed); draw((3,0)--(3,4),blue+linewidth(1)); label(&quot;$\\frac{s}{4}$&quot;,(0.5,4),N); label(&quot;$\\frac{s}{2}$&quot;,(2,4),N); label(&quot;$\\frac{s}{4}$&quot;,(3.5,4),N); label(&quot;$s$&quot;,(0,2),W); [/asy]\" width=\"242\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the side length of the square. After being cut, the paper will be separated into two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/cea3c0c9198336fc978d8ea30db28aa2168a5ea7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\times \\frac{s}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"34\" /> rectangles and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/3/5337a7215b0c9cfdc2da243c71f32de29d9959eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\times \\frac{s}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"46\" height=\"34\" /> rectangle.  The larger rectangle has perimeter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/6/27693228669c1e19f526b73725bf0a6d6e618b2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\left(s + \\frac{s}{2}\\right) = 3s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"121\" height=\"35\" /> while the smaller rectangle has perimeter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dc6cafc76af719343ec2cb84aa0c656071a31e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\left(s + \\frac{s}{4}\\right) = \\frac{5s}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"125\" height=\"38\" />.  Therefore, the ratio of the perimeters is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/e/6ae3baa898f62eb7c05101c3a5c977eb6ee3a763.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{5s}{2}\\right) \\div (3s) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{5}{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"185\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~DuoDuoling0, edited by j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose the square has side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  Then the paper would be separated into two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/5/3e528443cd2fb44453e65fc68c74581129c4f80e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" /> rectangles and a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/5/495c45dde59928de3e09d9f0cccd8f2a8af8bee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> rectangle.  The larger rectangle has perimeter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/f/67f338a105dc324c5dc2bd928b4af2561aa33224.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(4 + 2) = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" /> and the smaller rectangle has perimeter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/4413a1b0f6920a5956020794db317a91be70ee6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(4 + 1) = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" />, so the ratio of the perimeters is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12f9e233a348bd08cda1b5830209445f3686489e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10}{12} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{5}{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"106\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME\" title=\"1989 AJHSME\">1989 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_8_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 8 Problems and Solutions\"> All AJHSME/AMC 8 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017181531\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 135/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1967/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 132/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3461/5